# Ship system (design lock)

Status: **v0 composition + catalog + flagship outfit UI** — ship instances + in-port fleet compose + flagship mesh + `DT_Ships` + port **改装** schematic. No build rules, ship trade, 改造, or 改装 stats.

## Role

- **船** = world entity (`UShipObject` in `UShipManagerSubsystem`).
- At sea the unit of presence is always **Fleet**. No `AShip`. A one-ship group still appears as a fleet.
- `AFleet` mesh = **flagship** catalog mesh. Flagship is designated on the fleet (`FlagshipShipId`), not stored as a second truth on the ship.

## Architecture

| Piece | Path / type |
|----|-----|
| Object | `UShipObject` — `Source/.../Ship/` |
| Manager | `UShipManagerSubsystem` |
| Settings | `UShipManagerSettings` |
| Types | `ShipTypes.h` (`Ship_<N>`, `ShipType_TempCog` / `TempCaravel` / `TempCarrack`) |
| Catalog | `DT_Ships` / `FShipDefinition` — `Content/Ship/` |
| Tools | `Tools/CreateShipsDataTable.py` → `/Game/Ship/DT_Ships` |
| UI | city port `UCityPortWidget` + `UFleetManagementWidget` + flagship outfit `UShipOutfitWidget` under city panel |
| Save | `FShipSaveData` in `SaveTypes.h` (schema **v7**) |

Logic only at sea — **no `AShip`**.

## Ids & identity

- Ship Id: `Ship_<序号>` (serial). Fleet Id: `Fleet_<序号>`. **No** `Fleet_Player_*` as a player mark.
- Player command: `UFleetManagerSubsystem::PlayerCommandedFleetId`.
- Player company ownership: `OwnerCompanyId == Company_Player`.
- Pre-company: `OwnerCharacterId ==` player character (ships and fleets).
- Company still uses reserved Id `Company_Player`.

## Instance fields

| Field | Lock |
|----|-----|
| `ShipId` / `ShipTypeId` / `DisplayName` | Serial id; catalog type; numbered placeholder name |
| `OwnerCompanyId` / `OwnerCharacterId` | Company / pre-company player; both none = for-sale (later) |
| `FleetId` | Empty = ungrouped |
| `HostCityId` | Ungrouped → that city's **harbor**. Shipyard-finished ships also go to harbor. `Berth` not in v0 |

Catalog `FShipDefinition` in **`DT_Ships`**: type id, display name, mesh, `BaseSpeed`, `BaseStrength`. Instance does not store speed/strength. Placeholder rows: `ShipType_TempCog` (柯克, claim hull), `ShipType_TempCaravel` (卡拉维尔, `Ship2` mesh), `ShipType_TempCarrack` (克拉克, temp reuse Cog mesh). Missing table → built-in Cog fallback. Edit hulls in the DataTable, not C++. Rebuild rows: `Tools/CreateShipsDataTable.py`.

## Ungrouped / ownership

- Not in a fleet → must sit in a city harbor (exceptions later).
- Company-paid build → company owns (build later). Claimed starter → player character; founding company transfers those ships into `Company_Player`.
- Dissolve fleet only **in port**; ships stay company-owned at local harbor. Harbor cap later (infinite now).

## Composition (in port)

- City panel → 港口 → 港口 UI → 舰队管理.
- Layout: two columns (ships | personnel). Flagship slot and commander slot pinned top, highlighted. Overlay replaces the columns for fleet list / edit ships / commander pick.
- Fleet list: fleets **in this city**. `[+]` create; **Cancel = create nothing**. New-fleet draft pre-fills appointable player as commander and **ungrouped** harbor ships only (does not steal from other fleets).
- Max ships per fleet **32** (temp).
- Flagship slot fixed top; empty prompt: must designate flagship. Click a listed ship to set flagship (drag later).
- Edit ships: this city, owner-available (including ships already in company/player fleets here). Toggle in/out of **current** draft; overlay Confirm writes the draft.
- Personnel: **flagship posts only** (not one person per ship). Commander slot on top. Pool: company employees if founded; else player + companions.
- **Confirm** atomic: reject if no flagship or no commander.
- Reset restores draft. Cancel closes without write.
- First successful player compose writes `PlayerCommandedFleetId` (later fleets do not steal command).
- Stealing ships / commander / flagship from another **own** fleet leaves that fleet **illegal in port**. Do not auto-repair. Illegal: cannot leave port, cannot MoveTo, NpcAi will not dispatch.
- At sea: may retarget flagship **within** the fleet (commander auto-moves to new flagship 舰长室). No add/remove ships (remove = abandon, later). Capture later if world positions match.

## Flagship

- Legal fleet: exactly one flagship. Illegal in-port fleets may have none.
- Scene mesh always follows flagship when legal.
- Sink with remaining ships: pause, designate immediately (player / AI).
- Last ship sunk: fleet destroyed; survivors → HQ, or nearest port else London if no company. Claim-at-harbor is the wipe fallback (same as starter claim: eligible when player owns **zero** ships).

## Derived fleet stats (v0)

- Speed = slowest ship `BaseSpeed`.
- Strength = sum of ship `BaseStrength`.
- Officer modifiers later.

## Posts

- Command authority stays on fleet 司令.
- v0: flagship 舰长室 occupant **is** 司令 (bridge extra 司令 slot later).
- Other ships: no post assignment this slice.

## Outfit UI (in port, v0)

- City panel → 港口 → **改装** (`UShipOutfitWidget`). Close returns to port.
- **No character 3D** on the fleet mesh. Posts use a **2D outfit schematic** + **avatar icons** on slot anchors (see **Outfit schematic** below).
- Flagship schematic. **舰长室** (highlighted) = 司令. **甲板** = 水手长, **炮位** = 炮长, **制图室** = 领航员.
- Click a staffed compartment → pick from the same appoint pool as compose; Confirm writes the live fleet post (not a compose draft). 司令 replace-only (no 卸任). Other posts may 卸任.
- Locked placeholders: **瞭望塔**, **船帆**, **火炮配置** — no appoint, no stats.
- Target fleet: player commanded fleet in this city, else first owned fleet here.
- Does **not** create Facility `HostKind = Ship` objects this slice.

## Outfit schematic (2D — character slots)

**Split from 3D hull:** strategic map = `AFleet` + hull/sail/flag meshes. In-port **改装** = one **matching 2D diagram** per ship type + **named slot anchors** for icons. Diagram is **UI art**, not a StaticMesh socket.

