### Mast Rig packages (scheme A — v0 lock)

Each active `MastRig_XX` uses **three whole StaticMeshes** (mast + yards + sail + minimal rigging in one package):

```text
SM_<ShipType>_MastRig01_<RigType>_Full
SM_<ShipType>_MastRig01_<RigType>_Half
SM_<ShipType>_MastRig01_<RigType>_Furled
```

`<RigType>` = **`Square` | `Lateen`** (phase-one production) | **`Gaff`** (compatible, deferred). **Rig change = swap all three meshes** — not material-only.

- **Active rig:** one RigType triplet visible at a time on `Attach_MastRig_01`.
- Same pivot, transform, hang point within each triplet; **one state** visible at a time.
- Topgallants / royals: **no extra gameplay slot** — baked into the same package (Basic vs Advanced rig = different mesh triplets).
- Logic roles `Fore` / `Main` / `Mizzen` live in **data**, not socket names. Mizzen is still `MastRig_XX`.

#### Flag socket — on MastRig mesh (program lock **A**)

| Socket | Host mesh | Notes |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| `Attach_Flag` | **Active MastRig StaticMesh** (not Hull) | Main-mast top; independent flag mesh + MI. **Hide flag** when rig hidden / mast broken. |

Hierarchy: `Hull` → child at `Attach_MastRig_01` → MastRig mesh → child at `Attach_Flag`.

Validate: **Warning** if `Attach_Flag` missing on each imported MastRig triplet used by the type.

